From 6eb316fbb6ba01ca25ddebc7338f5d813331b719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OreoYang <oreo.yang@vecima.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:46:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] validation FEATURE incremental validation driven by an edit
 diff

Validate only what an edit diff can have changed instead of the whole module.
lyd_validate_module_incr() builds a scope from the diff (the outermost list
instances around a change, the schema nodes created or modified, and the
nodes outside those roots whose cross-instance when/must/leafref/unique
constraints a change can reach), checked against a per-context dependency
index (validation_deps.c). Constraints that cannot be proven unaffected, and
whole-module questions the index cannot analyse, fall back to the full
lyd_validate_module(), also when the validation itself deletes a node
(late fallback). Counters are exposed through lyd_validate_incr_stats() and
lyd_validate_incr_late_stats().

Safety rules, each with a test in tests/utests/data/test_validation_incr.c:
- creation of a node is skipped only for constraints that cannot turn false
  by it; not(), count(), != over an absolute path, first-node functions and
  arithmetic disable that skip
- value-keyed uniqueness-count must expressions are skipped by value
- a create on an implicit default counts as a modification
- a replace without orig-value, a require-instance config instance-identifier
  and a very deep delete chain are handled without losing a check
